  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1053 PM CDT FRI SEP 25 2026\n\nHigh pressure building over the region will deliver pleasant, dry\nweather through the weekend, with high temperatures ranging from\nthe upper 70s to mid 80s and overnight lows falling into the mid\n50s to low 60s. Drier air and increased subsidence will keep\nconditions rain-free into early next week. Although a weak\nshortwave moves into the Tennessee Valley on Monday and Tuesday,\nfollowed by a stronger upper trough late in the week, limited\nmoisture will preserve dry conditions through midweek. Shower and\nthunderstorm chances return late in the week as the upper trough\nand associated cold front approach Central Alabama.\n\nA return to southerly flow early next week will bring warmer\ntemperatures to the area. Highs are expected to rebound into the\nupper 80s and lower 90s by Tuesday, with near-90-degree heat\npersisting through the remainder of the workweek.\n\n16",
